# Help: Runtime verification (RV) with every monitor and reactor
#
# RV checks the kernel's behaviour against formal models while it runs:
# each monitor follows the events of one model and a reactor reacts
# when the kernel strays from it, by printing or by panicking. The
# monitors of kernel/trace/rv/monitors/ cover preemption, wakeups, the
# scheduler, real-time tasks and deadline tasks, and their KUnit tests
# and the reactors' run as modules.
#
# RV_PER_TASK_MONITORS caps how many per-task monitors run at once,
# each in a slot of every task; the sched and rtapp monitors need at
# least three, and the fragment takes the most RV allows, eight. The
# pagefault monitor is for x86 and RISC-V only.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - PREEMPT with PREEMPT_TRACER, and IRQSOFF_TRACER, for the preemption
#   and interrupt events of the wip and sts monitors.
# - KUNIT for the tests.
#
# The tests are loaded on demand; no builtin/ counterpart needed.
# See: kernel/trace/rv/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/trace/rv/index.html

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_FTRACE=y
CONFIG_PREEMPT=y
CONFIG_PREEMPT_TRACER=y
CONFIG_IRQSOFF_TRACER=y
CONFIG_KUNIT=y

#
# Monitors
#
CONFIG_RV=y
CONFIG_RV_PER_TASK_MONITORS=8
CONFIG_RV_MON_WIP=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_WWNR=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_SCHED=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_SCO=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_SNROC=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_SCPD=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_SNEP=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_STS=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_NRP=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_SSSW=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_OPID=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_RTAPP=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_PAGEFAULT=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_SLEEP=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_WAKEUP=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_STALL=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_DEADLINE=y
CONFIG_RV_MON_NOMISS=y

#
# Reactors and tests
#
CONFIG_RV_REACTORS=y
CONFIG_RV_REACT_PRINTK=y
CONFIG_RV_REACT_PANIC=y
CONFIG_RV_REACTORS_KUNIT=m
CONFIG_RV_MONITORS_KUNIT_TEST=m
